    "finding": "The old companion target has a broad horizontal eight-native-pixel bar with shallow one-pixel bottom lugs. Its complete contour matches same-page first-he patah in הַלְלוּיָהּ, whose bar also carries an ordinary shallow bottom lobe. Same-word yod qamats has a substantially deeper central stem, printed as a separate lower rectangle in this impression. The target is the patah bar morphology; its shallow lugs are ordinary print texture, not that qamats stem. The savedPSIK target and same controls show an agreeing flat bar/deep-stem distinction but are comparison only. Adjacent mem tsere is a narrower separated pair and cannot be the broad continuous het vowel bar.",
